    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\sigma_{G}^{2} $ is the total genetic variance, and $ \\sigma_{E_{c}}^{2} $ (MZ) is the variance due to common familial environment. The genetic covariance between monozygotic twins is equal to the total genetic variance because of the complete genetic identity of the individuals involved. For dizygotic twins,",
