    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Separate notation is needed for the variance due to common familial environment because it is not necessarily the same in the two types of twins. Since $ \\sigma_{z}^{2} = \\sigma_{b}^{2} + \\sigma_{e}^{2} $, it follows that the remainder of the phenotypic variance is in the within-pair component. Therefore,",
